Task: Read the financial-year start from the user's profile on the Rent tab
Track: rent_fy_grouping_20260907 — Phase 2
Verification tier: 2 (data flow)

WHAT CHANGED
- app/(dashboard)/properties/[propertyId]/(tabs)/rent/page.tsx: added a profiles
  select for financial_year_start_month/_day to the existing Promise.all, and
  derived fyStartMonth/fyStartDay with a fallback to AU_FY_START_MONTH/DAY.
  Passed both to RentalPaymentsSection.
- components/rental-payments-section.tsx: accepts fyStartMonth and fyStartDay.
  Not yet consumed — the grouping task later in this phase uses them.

WHY
The financial-year boundary is the user's, not a constant. Hardcoding 1 July would
make this tab and the tax pack disagree about which year a payment belongs to for
any user on a different year start. The tax-pack page already reads the profile;
this makes the Rent tab consistent with it rather than inventing a second rule.

The select joins the existing Promise.all rather than being awaited separately, so
no serial round trip is added to the page. maybeSingle() is used so a missing
profile row yields null instead of raising.

